# The end of the day (v1.0). Lowry stands down at once; pokes skip to
# the scene (dy_i=5: Isobel brought in, three pages) and write nine of
# Lyle's notes (three spectral among them, and the churchgoing). Mayor
# Ellis: P to his thirty, the record, 8 (the thirty women), HOLD, SIR!:
# the question, his answer, Ormsby, the note; the bench drops a band (his
# HOLD costs 3). X Y: no more witnesses. Lyle's charge: the notes in
# order over two pages, then the spectral evidence put down and the
# churchgoing; Ormsby's charge, shaken; the jury; the verdict one at a
# time: Janet Boyd and Bessie Shaw acquitted, the rest guilty; "Some are
# acquitted"; the pillory; what happened in 1711; the credits.
